    "config": "A0_dense_starter",
    "model": "gpt-4.1-mini",
    "agent_version": 1,
    "status": "answered",
    "answer": "The Intermediate Value Theorem states that if a function is continuous on [a, b] and takes values f(a) and f(b), then it takes every value between f(a) and f(b) at some point in (a, b). If f(0) > 0 and f(2) > 0, the theorem does not guarantee a zero in [0, 2], nor does it prove that there is no zero. It only applies to values between f(0) and f(2), so if both are positive, the theorem cannot be used to conclude the existence or nonexistence of zeros in the interval [openstax-calc1-p196-struct-02][openstax-calc1-p197-struct-01].",
